<title>PORTUGAL: Telecel sees revenues above 80 bln esc in '97.</title>
<headline>Telecel sees revenues above 80 bln esc in '97.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese mobile phone operator Telecel-Comunicacoes Pessoais expects to post total revenues of more than 80 billion escudos in 1997 and have more than 550,000 clients, its president Antonio Carrapatoso said.</p>
<p>Telecel had total revenues of 58.8 billion escudos in 1996.</p>
<p>Carrapatoso told a news conference that his forecast for the number of clients in 1997 was &quot;quite cautious, but the figure could be higher.&quot;</p>
<p>In 1996, the number of clients was 331,388.</p>
</text>
